# The Windows pools `.\windows-pools.ps1 autoscale` resizes. One line per pool:
#
#   cp windows-autoscale.conf.example windows-autoscale.conf   # gitignored, edit freely
#
# The Windows counterpart of autoscale.conf, and separate from it for the
# same reason windows-pools.conf is separate from pools.conf: a name like
# cicaid-pro can be a Linux pool and a Windows pool on the same host.
#
# <name> must also be declared in windows-pools.conf, which still supplies
# the repo; its count there is ignored while it's autoscaled. <min> is kept
# running even with nothing queued. [idle_minutes] is how long a pool must
# have no busy runner and no queued job before it drops back to <min>; 10 if
# omitted.
#
# name               min  max  idle_minutes
jobtrack             0    2
cicaid-pro           1    2    15
